  "notes": [
   "The step 1 parts list was correct, so no parts were added or dropped.",
   "The image's top half of the breadboard is labelled rows j to f, so I mapped it to catalogue bank 'b' (rows f-j). The image's bottom half is rows e to a, which I mapped to bank 't'. The ground rail drawn at the top of the image is therefore named 'bn'.",
   "Rail hole numbers (bn.1, bn.6, bn.13, bn.20) are estimated from the picture. All holes in one rail are a single strip, so the exact numbers don't change the circuit.",
   "Each channel works like this: an Arduino pin (8, 7 or 6) goes by a jumper wire to row e of column 8, 17 or 25. A 100 ohm resistor spans the centre gap from that column's row e to its row f. The speaker's red lead sits in row g of the same column, which is the same strip as row f. The speaker's black lead goes to the ground rail. The speaker is not polarized, so its ports 1 and 2 are interchangeable.",
   "Arduino GND (the pin next to AREF, taken as GND.1) goes by a black jumper wire to the ground rail.",
   "The manual's parts list and circuit text say 100 ohm resistors, but the schematic labels them 10k. I kept 100 ohm, following the parts list."
